WEBVTT

00:00:00.543 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.618 --> 00:00:06.185
In this lesson, we cut a mid fade, down to the skin at the very bottom,

00:00:06.135 --> 00:00:08.030
blending softly into the top.

00:00:08.459 --> 00:00:12.440
The client wants about five centimeters left on top, combed back,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.710
slightly to the side.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.590
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:16.839 --> 00:00:17.790
Here, we do it.

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:18.999
Step one:

00:00:19.241 --> 00:00:20.039
preparation.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.479
Wash your hands.

00:00:21.656 --> 00:00:22.193
Clippers,

00:00:22.143 --> 00:00:26.358
guards and combs have been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:00:26.788 --> 00:00:28.359
Fit a new blade in the razor.

00:00:28.656 --> 00:00:32.199
Wrap a disposable neck strip, and only then fasten the cape.

00:00:32.858 --> 00:00:33.637
Step two:

00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:35.877
the consultation, and choosing the height.

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:39.516
Ask whether the client wants a low, mid, or high fade,

00:00:39.466 --> 00:00:42.197
and whether he wants to see skin at the bottom.

00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:44.917
Point directly at the head, in the mirror:

00:00:45.266 --> 00:00:46.597
the fade will start here.

00:00:46.858 --> 00:00:50.917
How much to leave on top, you agree as in the men's haircut basics lesson.

00:00:51.403 --> 00:00:52.997
Then feel the head shape:

00:00:53.214 --> 00:00:59.237
find the parietal ridge, the occipital bone, flat spots, scars, and whorls.

00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:02.997
If the scalp has a wound or inflammation, don't shave close.

00:01:03.298 --> 00:01:06.837
For a client having his first fade, suggest starting a little lower.

00:01:07.072 --> 00:01:08.837
Going higher next time is easy.

00:01:09.024 --> 00:01:11.637
Once it is high, you have to wait for it to grow.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.088
Step three:

00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:14.448
set the guideline.

00:01:14.839 --> 00:01:15.968
Comb the hair down;

00:01:16.221 --> 00:01:17.888
the hair should be dry and clean.

00:01:18.237 --> 00:01:20.208
Fit the guard you chose for the guideline.

00:01:20.558 --> 00:01:24.528
Place the guard flat at the hairline, and move up, against the growth.

00:01:25.028 --> 00:01:27.648
At the agreed height, flick the clipper outward.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.168
Keep the wrist loose:

00:01:29.357 --> 00:01:31.888
the flick comes from the wrist, not the whole arm.

00:01:32.247 --> 00:01:33.488
Go all around the head:

00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:37.648
this side, the back, then the other side, at the same height.

00:01:38.071 --> 00:01:40.768
Near the ear, fold the ear down gently.

00:01:41.027 --> 00:01:43.968
At the back, the guideline follows the head shape.

00:01:44.391 --> 00:01:47.819
If the head is flat at the back, drop the guideline a little there,

00:01:47.769 --> 00:01:48.928
to keep the roundness.

00:01:49.277 --> 00:01:51.488
After going all the way around, check:

00:01:51.895 --> 00:01:54.768
is the guideline straight, and even on both sides?

00:01:55.355 --> 00:01:56.223
Step four:

00:01:56.398 --> 00:01:57.583
below the guideline.

00:01:58.089 --> 00:02:00.703
Divide that area into two or three bands.

00:02:01.124 --> 00:02:04.855
For the bottom band, close the lever, or use a shorter guard,

00:02:04.805 --> 00:02:06.303
then take the guard off.

00:02:06.836 --> 00:02:09.095
Go up a shorter distance than the guideline,

00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:11.103
and flick out at the stopping point too.

00:02:11.604 --> 00:02:16.063
Around the ears and at the nape hairline, go very lightly, a little at a time.

00:02:16.405 --> 00:02:20.862
If the client wants it down to the skin, leave the fully bare part for later,

00:02:20.812 --> 00:02:21.663
in step seven.

00:02:21.915 --> 00:02:25.583
For now, you just need the bottom band very short and even.

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.186
Step five:

00:02:27.376 --> 00:02:28.626
blend each band.

00:02:29.132 --> 00:02:31.026
Now there are lines between the bands.

00:02:31.135 --> 00:02:32.466
We work from the bottom up.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.066
At the lowest line, use the length in between the two bands:

00:02:36.336 --> 00:02:37.746
open the lever halfway.

00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:42.306
Go only along the line, with a scooping motion outward, light and short.

00:02:42.815 --> 00:02:47.666
Then move up to the next line, and open the lever further, or fit a half-size guard.

00:02:47.891 --> 00:02:51.666
Keep going up to the guideline, and from the guideline up to the top.

00:02:51.924 --> 00:02:55.293
Between passes, brush off the loose hair with a brush,

00:02:55.243 --> 00:02:57.506
or blow it gently away with a dryer.

00:02:57.931 --> 00:03:02.386
Loose hair lying on the head hides the lines, and you think it is already smooth.

00:03:03.035 --> 00:03:03.998
Step six:

00:03:04.182 --> 00:03:05.998
erase any remaining lines.

00:03:06.173 --> 00:03:08.558
Comb the hair down, and look under the light.

00:03:08.916 --> 00:03:12.247
Wherever there is still a faint line, or a darker patch,

00:03:12.197 --> 00:03:14.238
use exactly the in-between length,

00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:15.998
and go only over that spot.

00:03:16.505 --> 00:03:18.318
Do not push the whole fade higher.

00:03:18.587 --> 00:03:19.838
Erase it where it is.

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:23.998
At a whorl at the nape, go in several directions, gently.

00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:26.638
The back is harder to see than the sides.

00:03:26.927 --> 00:03:28.158
Don't just look in the mirror.

00:03:28.412 --> 00:03:31.918
Walk around behind the client, bend down, and look.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:33.443
Step seven:

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.443
the skin part and the outline.

00:03:35.842 --> 00:03:40.163
Stretch the skin lightly, and use a foil shaver to clean up the very bottom.

00:03:40.573 --> 00:03:45.123
If you use a razor, only a new blade, with the grain, a single pass.

00:03:45.455 --> 00:03:49.283
If the skin turns red, or the client feels a sting, stop.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.283
Don't force it to be really close.

00:03:51.712 --> 00:03:55.814
Then outline around the ears, the sideburns, and the nape with a trimmer,

00:03:55.764 --> 00:03:57.923
as in the men's haircut basics lesson.

00:03:58.183 --> 00:03:59.283
A natural outline;

00:03:59.391 --> 00:04:00.403
don't cut it too high.

00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:01.842
Step eight:

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:02.642
check.

00:04:03.031 --> 00:04:05.842
Bring the client into good light, or turn on the lamp.

00:04:06.252 --> 00:04:09.442
Have the client sit up straight, looking straight into the mirror.

00:04:09.776 --> 00:04:11.042
Compare both sides:

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.762
the fade at the same height, the sideburns even.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.782
If one side is higher, you can't bring it down anymore,

00:04:16.732 --> 00:04:18.402
because the hair is already short.

00:04:18.815 --> 00:04:21.522
The only way is to raise the lower side to match.

00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:24.402
So be careful right from the moment you set the guideline.

00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:28.583
Then look from the left, from the right, crouch down to eye level,

00:04:28.533 --> 00:04:29.762
and look at the back.

00:04:30.271 --> 00:04:32.322
Ask the client to tilt his head slightly:

00:04:32.591 --> 00:04:35.122
small lines show up more clearly under the light.

00:04:35.547 --> 00:04:38.082
Wherever it is not yet smooth, fix it right away.

00:04:38.661 --> 00:04:39.518
Step nine:

00:04:39.782 --> 00:04:40.878
connect to the top.

00:04:41.405 --> 00:04:44.958
Cut the top from a guideline, as in the men's haircut basics lesson.

00:04:45.387 --> 00:04:49.353
Then blend where the fade meets the top, with scissor over comb,

00:04:49.303 --> 00:04:50.638
or clipper over comb.

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:54.389
The comb moves up steadily, never staying in one spot,

00:04:54.339 --> 00:04:57.358
until you run your hand up and there is no ridge.

00:04:57.527 --> 00:05:00.297
The shorter the top, the smoother the blend must be,

00:05:00.247 --> 00:05:03.278
because there is no long hair falling over it to hide it.

00:05:03.858 --> 00:05:04.732
Step ten:

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:05.692
the finish.

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:07.692
Brush off all the loose hair.

00:05:08.109 --> 00:05:11.591
On the freshly shaved area, if the client has sensitive skin,

00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:14.572
you can apply a little fragrance-free soothing cream,

00:05:14.607 --> 00:05:15.772
if the client agrees.

00:05:16.219 --> 00:05:19.852
Style the top with product, and show the client how to do it at home.

00:05:20.275 --> 00:05:24.652
Hold a hand mirror behind him, so the client can see both sides and the nape.

00:05:25.028 --> 00:05:26.092
Write it in the record:

00:05:26.348 --> 00:05:28.972
the height, the guards, the lever setting.

00:05:29.397 --> 00:05:30.332
Book the next visit;

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.132
many clients come back after two to three weeks.

00:05:33.546 --> 00:05:34.572
Let the client know:

00:05:34.761 --> 00:05:38.652
the bare part will start to grow out after a few days, and that is normal.

00:05:39.311 --> 00:05:40.666
After the client leaves:

00:05:40.736 --> 00:05:44.842
brush the hair out of the clipper blade, disinfect the blade, guards,

00:05:44.792 --> 00:05:47.546
combs and the shaver as the product instructs,

00:05:47.661 --> 00:05:48.666
and oil the blade.

00:05:49.175 --> 00:05:50.906
The same goes for the foil shaver:

00:05:51.175 --> 00:05:53.866
clean the foil and the cutter as the maker instructs.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:56.346
Razor blades go into the sharps container.

00:05:56.614 --> 00:05:59.546
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
